<body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
 {!indexable && <div class="dev">DESIGN PREVIEW · Orders and payments are inactive</div>}
 <div class="ribbon">A LITTLE SPACE FOR YOUR THOUGHTS, THROUGH CANCER AND BEYOND</div>
 <header><div class="nav"><a href="#home" class="logo"><img class="brand-lotus" src="/assets/verified/lotus.png" alt="" width="45" height="36"/> I WILL BLOOM</a><nav class="navlinks" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/journal/">The Journal</a><a href="/journal/#inside-pages">Inside the Pages</a><a href="/alettertoyou/">Our Story</a><a href="/bloom-library/">The Bloom Library</a></nav><a class="btn" href="#shop">Shop the journal →</a><details class="mobile-nav"><summary>Menu</summary><nav aria-label="Mobile navigation"><a href="/journal/">The Journal</a><a href="/alettertoyou/">Our Story</a><a href="/bloom-library/">Bloom Library</a><a href="/for-healthcare-pros/">Professionals</a><a href="/contactiwb/">Contact</a></nav></details></div></header>
 <main id="main">
  <section id="home" class="hero"><div class="container hero-inner"><div><div class="eyebrow">A gentle companion during cancer treatment</div><h1>Every thought deserves <em>somewhere gentle</em> to land.</h1><p>I made I Will Bloom because, during cancer treatment, I needed somewhere to put the thoughts I carried home from appointments. It’s a guided journal for those thoughts, the ordinary days and the small things you want to remember.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/journal/#order">Shop the journal · €38</a><a class="text-link" href="/journal/#inside-pages">Look inside →</a></div><div class="smallnote">Support for your mind — not just your schedule.</div></div><figure class="hero-photo"><img src="/assets/verified/journal-by-the-sea.webp" width="709" height="950" alt="Rachel holding the open I Will Bloom journal and a pen by the sea" fetchpriority="high"/></figure></div></section>
  <section id="shop" class="section product"><div class="container purchase"><figure class="product-photo"><img src="/assets/verified/journal-cover.webp" width="1080" height="1350" loading="lazy" alt="The physical I Will Bloom journal, held in one hand to show its size and spiral binding"/></figure><div class="copy"><h2>The I Will Bloom Journal</h2><p>A5 hardback, white spiral binding and gentle prompts for treatment and recovery. Explore the journal, its thoughtful extras and the pages inside.</p><div class="price">€38.00</div><a class="btn" href="/journal/#order">Shop the journal →</a><p><a href="/journal/" class="text-link">See what’s included →</a></p></div></div></section>
  <section id="inside" class="section">
    <div class="container inside-layout">
      <div class="copy">
        <h2>Inside the journal</h2>
        <p>Sometimes your mind needs more than blank pages. It needs structure.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/journal/#inside-pages">See the pages →</a>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Daily reflections</dt><dd>A little space for your thoughts, energy and everyday moments.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Colour &amp; Calm and Moments of Wonder</dt><dd>Colouring pages and short stories for when words feel hard to find.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Life Logistics and Load Lighteners</dt><dd>Prompts for the everyday tasks that carry on and the help you might welcome.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="story" class="section"><div class="container split"><div class="copy"><div class="eyebrow">A note from the founder</div><h2>Created with understanding. Made with care.</h2><p>Some days I wanted to write. Other days I just needed a little structure to get started. I wanted the journal to leave room for both.</p><p>If you’re here for someone you love, I know how hard it can be to find the words. The journal is a small way to say “I’m thinking of you” and give them something they can make their own.</p><a class="btn ghost" href="/alettertoyou/">Read my letter →</a></div><figure class="founder-photo"><img src="/assets/verified/rachel-writing-on-the-beach.webp" width="712" height="950" loading="lazy" alt="Rachel sitting on the sand and writing in her I Will Bloom journal"/><figcaption>Rachel writing in her journal</figcaption></figure></div></section>
  
  <section class="reader-note section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">A partner’s perspective</p><blockquote><p>“This journal provides a structured but gentle space that allows reflection without pressure.”</p><footer>Seamus L · Rachel’s husband</footer><p><a href="/testimonials/">Read the testimonial →</a></p></blockquote></div></section><section id="library" class="section"><div class="container center"><h2>The Bloom Library</h2><p class="intro">Helpful reading for the person navigating cancer, and for the people who want to support them.</p><div class="stories"><a class="story" href="/bloom-library/when-words-feel-difficult/"><h3>When words feel difficult</h3><p>A few gentle starting points for a page that feels hard to begin.</p></a><a class="story" href="/bloom-library/a-gift-without-expectations/"><h3>A gift without expectations</h3><p>Offering something thoughtful while leaving room for the person receiving it.</p></a><a class="story" href="/bloom-library/no-right-way-to-use-a-journal/"><h3>There is no right way to use a journal</h3><p>Skip a page. Write one word. Start again when you want to.</p></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container faq"><h2>Questions about the journal</h2><details><summary>Is this a medical journal?</summary><p>No. It offers guided reflection and practical space for everyday feelings. It does not provide medical advice or replace care from your healthcare team.</p></details><details><summary>Can I give it to someone I love?</summary><p>Yes. It is a thoughtful way to offer someone space for themselves, without expecting them to feel or respond in a particular way.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to write every day?</summary><p>No. Start wherever you like, skip pages, or return when you feel ready. The journal works at your pace.</p></details><details><summary>Do you work with professionals and organisations?</summary><p>We welcome enquiries from healthcare professionals, charities and organisations. <a href="mailto:connect@iwillbloom.com">Contact Rachel</a> about the journal and bulk purchases.</p></details></div></section>
 </main>
 <footer><div class="container foot"><div><a class="logo" href="#home"><img class="brand-lotus" src="/assets/verified/lotus.png" alt="" width="45" height="36"/> I WILL BLOOM</a><small>© I Will Bloom. Emotional support, not medical advice.</small></div><div><a href="/journal/">The Journal</a><a href="#library">Resources</a><a href="/contactiwb/">Contact</a><a href="/for-healthcare-pros/">Professionals</a></div></div></footer>
</body>
</html>
